WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:04.899
Dear Fellow Scholars, this is Two Minute Papers
with Károly Zsolnai-Fehér.

00:00:04.899 --> 00:00:10.670
Some people say that the most boring thing
is watching paint dry. They have clearly not

00:00:10.670 --> 00:00:15.769
seen this amazing research work, that makes
it possible to simulate the entire process

00:00:15.769 --> 00:00:17.530
of painting on a canvas.

00:00:17.530 --> 00:00:22.060
We have covered plenty of papers in fluid
simulations, and this is no exception - I

00:00:22.060 --> 00:00:26.920
admit that I am completely addicted and just
can't help it. Maybe I should seek professional

00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:27.770
assistance.

00:00:27.770 --> 00:00:34.280
So, as there is a lot of progress in simulating
the motion of fluids, and paint is a fluid,

00:00:34.280 --> 00:00:38.010
then why not simulate the process of painting
on a canvas?

00:00:38.010 --> 00:00:43.030
The simulations with this technique are so
detailed that even the bristle interactions

00:00:43.030 --> 00:00:47.760
are taken into consideration, therefore one
can capture artistic brush stroke effects

00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:53.710
like stabbing. Stabbing, despite the horrifying
name, basically means shoving the brush into

00:00:53.710 --> 00:00:57.270
the canvas and rotating it around to get cool effect.

00:00:57.270 --> 00:01:02.289
The fluid simulation part includes paint adhesion
and is so detailed that it can capture the

00:01:02.289 --> 00:01:08.030
well-known impasto style where paint is applied
to the canvas in such large chunks, they are

00:01:08.030 --> 00:01:13.630
so thick that one can see all the strokes
that have been made. And all this is done

00:01:13.630 --> 00:01:17.340
in real-time. Amazing results.

00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:24.200
Traditional techniques cannot even come close
to simulating such sophisticated effects.

00:01:24.200 --> 00:01:28.659
As it happened many times before in computer
graphics: just put such a powerful algorithm

00:01:28.659 --> 00:01:53.299
into the hands of great artists and enjoy
the majestic creations they give birth to.

00:01:53.299 --> 00:01:57.060
Thanks for watching and for your generous
support, and I'll see you next time!

